 "script": {
  "hook": "The badge says nine, the chat shows five. Which is wrong?",
  "question": "Design chat list pagination and unread counts.",
  "trap": "The trap: count unread from loaded messages. Older pages are missing, so the count lies.",
  "steps": [
   "Cursor paging. Page by last activity time, so new messages never shift the pages.",
   "Counter per chat. The server owns the unread count, stored beside the last read sequence.",
   "Optimistic read. Opening a chat zeroes the count locally, then syncs. Newer sequence wins.",
   "Badge sync. The badge is the sum of the counters, muted chats excluded."
  ],
  "takeaway": "The server counts. The client pages. Compare by sequence.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: Notification dedupe and badge counts.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
